@startuml
skinparam defaultFontName Nanum Gothic
skinparam shadowing false
title 채팅의 선택 약 / 시간대 확인 요청과 환자 완료
actor Caregiver
actor Patient
boundary "LinkedChatUI (caregiver)" as Sender
control "ManageLinkedChat (server)" as Chat
database "Chat messages + push jobs" as Messages
boundary "LinkedChatUI (patient)" as Receiver
control "LinkedChatDoseRecorder" as Recorder
participant "DoseSyncService" as Sync
database "Encrypted dose outbox" as Store
control "SyncDose" as Server

Caregiver -> Sender: Select saved medications and request a medication check
Sender -> Chat: medication_check_request + medication IDs + optional slot
Chat -> Chat: Active link, caregiver role, patient ownership and active medications
Chat -> Chat: Snapshot only selected medicines due today in requested slots
note right of Chat: PRN/rest-day attachments do not gain scheduled dose actions.\nNo search references, place/history/source-alert context mixing.\nSame ID with changed body/ID set/slot or deleted request is a conflict.
Chat -> Messages: Persist request and delivery job
Messages --> Receiver: Existing delivery/history path
Receiver -> Recorder: confirmationContexts(message, user, patient, day)
Recorder --> Receiver: Only incoming explicit current-day request slots
note over Receiver,Recorder: Also supports existing slot_check_request snapshots.\nNo actions for ordinary text, other roles, old days or deleted messages.
Patient -> Receiver: Tap one slot's completion button
Receiver -> Recorder: Load current schedules
Recorder --> Receiver: Current authorized dose contexts
Receiver -> Receiver: Recheck message, link, account, day and current completion state
Receiver -> Recorder: Plan only original requested medicines in tapped slot
alt Current schedule still supports selection
Recorder -> Sync: Record same-account dose intent (existing app path)
Sync -> Store: Durable operation ID and pending state
Store --> Receiver: Local saved / awaiting sync; keep composer draft
Sync -> Server: Existing completion-operations request
Server -> Server: Validate ownership, date, regimen revision; apply once
Server --> Sync: Receipt + schedule (+ chat receipt when link permits)
Sync -> Store: Atomic ACK + authoritative cache
Sync --> Receiver: Confirmed state
else Scope or schedule changed
Receiver -> Patient: Recheck schedule; do not broaden to other drugs/slots
end
note over Store,Server: Local save is not server acknowledgement.\nRetries use existing stable IDs; caregiver never writes the patient's dose.\nA lost link after durable recording may omit chat while validating own dose.
@enduml
